    "_note": "Chapter 34, Lesson 2 (ch34-l02) — the core table: one sound Form I model, كَتَبَ → يَكْتُبُ, in five readings (أَنَا، نَحْنُ، هُوَ، أَنْتَ، هِيَ) on four prefix patterns أ ن ي ت. أَنْتَ and هِيَ share تَكْتُبُ and are practised separately in named contexts; no isolated تَكْتُبُ is ever keyed to one subject. أَنْتِ (تَكْتُبِينَ) is left to Chapter 37. Rebuilt 2026-10-02 in the proposal harvest, batch 2 (Docs/proposals/proposal-harvest-tracker.md), from Docs/proposals/chapter-34-content-proposal.md and its review amendments: the imperfect in context — not 'only right now' but unfinished or habitual action, shown by الْآنَ / كُلَّ يَوْمٍ; five subject readings on one sound Form I model (أَكْتُبُ، نَكْتُبُ، يَكْتُبُ، and تَكْتُبُ for أَنْتَ and for هِيَ) — four prefix patterns, with تَكْتُبُ decided by context; transfer to supplied complete imperfects (يَذْهَبُ، يَجْلِسُ، يَعْلَمُ — the middle vowel is given, never guessed); لَا + imperfect for 'does not', with 'Do not!' (لَا تَجْلِسْ، 9:40 لَا تَحْزَنْ) as a recognition contrast only (Chapter 45 teaches it); an object, an object pronoun and a time word; review; 12-question test. نَعْبُدُ is Chapter 10 retrieval; نَسْتَعِينُ is glossed (root ع و ن). The future (سَـ / سَوْفَ) is Chapter 35; أَنْتِ forms are Chapter 37. The old Al-Fatiha capstone ch34-l07 is kept as a DRAFT row at order 8 so no earlier completion counts as passing the new test. Removed: 'present tense = right now', the six-row 'full table', four prefixes read as four subjects, أَفْعَلُ as a pattern for every verb, نَسْتَعِينُ under س-ع-ن, the ash-Sharh line cited as 1:6, نَرَانِي, many-to-one matching, multi-word build tiles and out-of-range reveal highlights.",
